1z3b|n|of Stand ; The act of stopping, or coming to a stand; the state of being erect upon the feet; stand. ; Maintenance of position; duration; duration or existence in the same place or condition; continuance; as, a custom of long standing; an officer of long standing. ; Place to stand in; station; stand. ; Condition in society; relative position; reputation; rank; as, a man of good standing, or of high standing.	a:w2z,22,5~w2z,22,5	n:ecg,27,2~ecg,27,2
