1z9n|a|Firm in standing or position; not tottering or shaking; fixed; firm. ; Constant in feeling, purpose, or pursuit; not fickle, changeable, or wavering; not easily moved or persuaded to alter a purpose; resolute; as, a man steady in his principles, in his purpose, or in the pursuit of an object. ; Regular; constant; undeviating; uniform; as, the steady course of the sun; a steady breeze of wind.	j:1zxw,115,19;1n80,68,3;1z6q,48,2;22wi,33,3~1zxw,115,19;1n80,68,3;22wi,33,3;1z6q,48,2
