1zel|a|To move the foot in walking; to advance or recede by raising and moving one of the feet to another resting place, or by moving both feet in succession. ; To walk; to go on foot; esp., to walk a little distance; as, to step to one of the neighbors. ; To walk slowly, gravely, or resolutely. ; Fig.: To move mentally; to go in imagination.	j:v5q,28,1~v5q,28,1
